#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074957 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll consider real-life situations where we have to multiply fractions by whole numbers.\n\nSuppose that Justin, a chef, has $8$ large tins of tomatoes. If each tin of tomatoes weighs\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{4}\\,\\textrm{lb}\n$$\n\nhow many pounds of tomatoes does Justin have in total?\n\nTo find out the total weight of tomatoes, we need to multiply\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{4}\\,\\textrm{lb}\n$$\n\nby $8$.\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n8 \\times \\dfrac54= \\dfrac{8\\times 5}{4} = \\dfrac{40}4\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by interpreting the fraction as a division:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{40}{4} = 40 \\div 4 = 10\n$$\n\nSo, in total, Justin has $10\\,\\textrm{lb}$ of tomatoes." :tutorial/id #uuid "298ab81d-8afe-5255-bdcd-354d669f8700" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1886 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
